.TH NUSA\-RG 1 "2026-10-18" "termux-nusa-rg 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nusa\-rg \- coding assistant for Termux with local\-project RAG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nusa\-rg
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nusa\-rg
indexes a local project into SQLite FTS5, retrieves the most relevant code
snippets for each question, and answers through either an external LLM API or a
local llama.cpp model. It is designed for ARM64 Android devices running Termux.
.PP
All state is kept under
.IR ~/.nusa\-rg/ ,
or the directory named by
.BR NUSA_RG_HOME .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B chat [\fIMESSAGE\fR] [options]
Start an interactive chat session, or answer a single message and exit.
Inside a session,
.BR /exit ,
.BR /quit ,
.BR /clear ,
.BR "/caveman [on|off]" ,
and
.B /help
are recognised, and Ctrl+D ends the session. End a line with
.B \\\\
to continue a multi\-line block terminated by a blank line. A line beginning
with
.B !
runs a terminal command (through
.B rtk
when installed) and keeps its output as context for the next question.
.br
Options:
.BR \-p ", " \-\-project " \fIPATH\fR"
.B \-\-no\-rag
skip retrieval;
.B \-\-stream
stream the API response;
.B \-\-index " / " \-\-no\-index
control automatic indexing;
.B \-\-caveman
answer in telegraphic style for this session;
.B \-\-plain
print raw Markdown.
.TP
.B run [options] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARG\fR ...]
Run a terminal command. When
.B rtk
(Rust Token Killer) is on the PATH the command is sent through it as
.IB rtk " COMMAND" ,
and rtk rewrites the output before it reaches the model; the output is capped
in bytes either way. The command line is never passed through a shell, and
shell operators are rejected with an explanation.
.br
Options:
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ask " \fIQUESTION\fR"
answer
.I QUESTION
with the command output attached as context;
.B \-\-raw
do not route the command through rtk;
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
override
.B command_timeout
for this run;
.BR \-p ", " \-\-project " \fIPATH\fR" ","
.BR \-\-no\-rag ", "
.BR \-\-stream ", "
.BR \-\-caveman ", "
.BR \-\-plain
as for
.BR chat .
The exit code is the command's own, so
.B run
composes with scripts.
.TP
.B index [\fIPATH\fR] [options]
Scan a project directory and write the chunks to the FTS5 index. The path
becomes
.BR default_project_path .
Options:
.B \-\-force
re\-index regardless of mtime,
.B \-\-json
emit statistics as JSON,
.B \-\-set\-default
keep the existing default project path.
.TP
.B config \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.TQ
.B config show [\-\-reveal]
Print the active configuration.
.B \-\-reveal
decrypts the API key; treat the output as sensitive.
.TQ
.B config set \fIKEY\fR [\fIVALUE\fR] [\-\-secret] [\-\-provider \fIPROVIDER\fR]
Set a value. Credential fields are stored encrypted.
.B \-\-secret
without a value prompts without echoing.
.B \-\-provider
stores
.B api_key
for one catalogue provider instead of the default slot.
Special keys:
.B provider
(accepts
.IR external ", " local ,
or any catalogue id),
.BR fallback_providers " (a comma\-separated list of \fIid\fR or \fIid:model\fR entries),"
.BR response_style " ("
.IR default " or " caveman ),
and
.BR api_key .
.TQ
.B config path
Print the resolved path of every state file.
.TP
.B providers \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.TQ
.B providers list [\fB\-\-search\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]
List the bundled catalogue of 200+ providers with their model counts. Only
OpenAI chat\-completions compatible providers are shown unless
.B \-\-all
is given; the others are listed for their key names and documentation but
cannot be called directly.
.TQ
.B providers show \fIPROVIDER\fR
Print one provider's endpoint, key environment variable, model count, and
default model, plus the command that switches to it.
.TQ
.B providers models \fIPROVIDER\fR [\fB\-\-search\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]
List the models a provider hosts, newest first, with context size and price
per million tokens when the catalogue knows them.
.TQ
.B providers refresh [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
Fetch a fresh catalogue (default: the models.dev registry) into the state
directory, replacing the bundled snapshot.
.TP
.B update [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Update a source checkout to the latest release and re\-run the installer.
Config, credentials and the index in ~/.nusa\-rg are never touched.
An installation made from a package manager cannot self\-update; the command
reports that and points at \fBpkg upgrade\fR. An update runs \fBgit reset \-\-hard\fR
against \fBorigin\fR, so a checkout whose remote is not
\fBgithub.com/PADZ\-PRD/RAG\-termux\-cli\fR is refused unless
\fBupdate_remote\fR names it, as in
\fBrad\-assist config set update_remote ~/RAG\-termux\-cli.git\fR for an offline
mirror. A dirty tree or a diverged branch stops the update unless
\fB\-\-force\fR is given.
.TP
.B status
Report the provider, model, response style, fallback chain, index size, and a
connectivity check.
.TP
.B doctor
Run installation and security self\-checks, including whether
.B rtk
is available and whether the provider catalogue loads. Exits non\-zero if any
fail.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help. Help text includes usage examples.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-colour
Disable ANSI colours. Also honours
.BR NO_COLOR .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NUSA_RG_HOME
Override the state directory. Default
.IR ~/.nusa\-rg .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables all ANSI colour output.
.TP
.B GROQ_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ...
Keys for catalogue providers are read from the environment variables models.dev
lists (shown by
.BR "nusa\-rg providers show \fIPROVIDER\fR" ),
after the per\-provider keystore entry and before the shared
.B api_key
slot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.nusa\-rg/config.yaml
Configuration. API keys appear only as
.B keystore://
references.
.TP
.I ~/.nusa\-rg/keystore.bin
AES\-256\-GCM sealed credentials.
.TP
.I ~/.nusa\-rg/index.db
SQLite FTS5 project index. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.nusa\-rg/catalog.json
Provider catalogue written by
.BR "nusa\-rg providers refresh" .
Optional; when present it overrides the bundled snapshot. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.nusa\-rg/logs/app.log
Operational log. Metadata only, mode 0600, rotated at 10 MB keeping 5 archives.
.TP
.I ~/.nusa\-rg/logs/audit.log
Audit trail for configuration changes and index operations.
.SH SECURITY
API keys are encrypted with AES\-256\-GCM and never written to
.I config.yaml
or to any log. Log entries record timestamps, levels, event names, and a
SHA\-256 fingerprint of queries rather than query text or code. Terminal
commands execute only when typed with
.B run
or
.BR !command ;
the command line is split into an argument list and never passed through a
shell, shell operators are rejected, and the output is byte\-capped,
delimited, and sanitised before it can reach a prompt. Control markers found
in indexed files or command output are neutralised before they can reach a
prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nusa\-rg index ~/projects/my\-app
Index a project directory.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg chat
Start an interactive session.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg chat "explain this traceback"
Answer a single question.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg providers list
Browse the bundled provider catalogue.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg config set provider deepseek
Switch to a catalogue provider; its default model is applied too.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg config set api_key \-\-provider groq \-\-secret
Store a key for one provider.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg run \-\-ask "what broke?" pytest \-x
Run a command and ask about its output.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg chat \-\-caveman
Start a session that answers in telegraphic style to save output tokens.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg config set provider local
Switch to the offline llama.cpp path.
.TP
.B nusa\-rg doctor
Verify the installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama (1),
.BR termux\-info (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/PADZ-PRD/RAG\-termux\-cli/issues